        "original_id": "9a6ff401-5982-51dc-b6ed-0f192cab5565",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Songs: \"Mmm Papi\", \"La Isla Bonita\", \"Whiplash\", \"Rock Me In\"\n- People: Madonna, Patrick Leonard, Bruce Gaitsch, Selena Gomez & the Scene\n- Albums: \"True Blue\"\n- Places: San Pedro Town\n- Topics: Latin pop influence, songwriting, inspiration\n\nFacts:\n- In 1984, San Pedro Town was granted town status.\n- In 1986, Madonna released \"La Isla Bonita\" on her third studio album \"True Blue\".\n- In 1986, Madonna and Patrick Leonard co-wrote and co-produced \"La Isla Bonita\", and Bruce Gaitsch contributed additional songwriting.\n- In 1987, \"La Isla Bonita\" was noted as a Madonna song with a Latin pop style.\n- San Pedro Town was sometimes said to have inspired \"La Isla Bonita\", which opens with the lyric \"last night I dreamt of San Pedro\".\n- \"Mmm Papi\" was noted for having a Latin pop influence similar to Madonna's \"La Isla Bonita\".\n- The same writers together wrote \"Mmm Papi\", \"Rock Me In\", and \"Whiplash\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
